Now we can use the ratio of the edges to find \( s_2 \):

\[
\frac{3}{1} = \frac{3}{s_2}
\]

This gives us \( s_2 = 1 \).

The volume of the second cube is \( V_2 = s_2^3 = 1^3 = 1 \).

