- \( x(t) \) is the position of the oscillator at time \( t \)
- \( A \) is the amplitude of the oscillator
- \( \phi \) is the phase phase
- \( x_0 \) is the initial position of the oscillator

The equation of motion for a damped harmonic oscillator is:

\[
\ddot{x} + \lambda \dot{x} + \lambda^2 x = 0
